>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `fast_tac`

``` hol4
classicalLib.fast_tac : clasetLib.claset -> NTactical.ntactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constructs the claset-explicit form of `FAST_TAC`.

`fast_tac cs` performs depth-first solve-completely search using `cs`. It
safely saturates states, expands the first goal, and commits to the
instantiating cascade whenever it has a candidate. Dynamic pruning removes
choices that cannot affect remaining goals. There is no depth or node
bound.

Unlike `FAST_TAC`, this interface takes a prepared classical rule set and
returns an ntactic without applying theorem-list markers or making the
result deterministic.

### Failure

Produces no result if search is exhausted without a complete proof. Search
can diverge, and replay failure is reported as an error.

### Example

``` hol4
val fast = classicalLib.fast_tac (clasetLib.the_claset ());
```

